1
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:10,790
<i>Thundershowers are 
expected in the Crocodile Falls area</i>

2
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:14,380
<i>and some of the surrounding gullies, 
so take out your...</i>

3
00:02:19,090 --> 00:02:21,050
COdyI

4
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:22,260
Yeah, Mom?

5
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:25,720
- What about your breakfast? 
- I've got some sandwiches in my pack.

6
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:29,230
- Be home for supper. 
- No worries, Mom.

7
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:48,290
I know, I'm coming.

8
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:51,540
Hustle up, Nelson. 
Faloo's sounding the call!

9
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:01,590
Come on, little Wombats, hurry!

10
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:17,860
Who's caught this time?

11
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,070
You don't know her, Cody.

12
00:03:19,150 --> 00:03:21,700
Her name is Marahute, 
the great golden eagle.

13
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:22,740
Where is she?

14
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:25,870
She's caught, high on a cliff 
in a poacher's trap.

15
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:28,700
- You're the only one who can reach her. 
- I'll get her loose.

16
00:03:28,790 --> 00:03:31,790
Righto. Hop on, no time to lose.

17
00:03:50,810 --> 00:03:54,980
She's up on top of that ridge. 
Be careful, little friend.

18
00:04:21,670 --> 00:04:23,680
Marahute!

19
00:04:35,350 --> 00:04:38,150
Calm down, calm down.

20
00:04:38,230 --> 00:04:39,900
I'm not gonna hurt you.

21
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:43,030
That's a girl. Stay still.

22
00:04:44,570 --> 00:04:46,530
It's okay.

23
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:51,950
No, wait! I'm here to help you.

24
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:54,710
Easy! Easy!

25
00:05:02,130 --> 00:05:03,670
You're free!

26
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:04,610
Higher!

27
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:12,450
You're a mom!

28
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:19,870
They're very warm. 
Are they gonna hatch soon?

29
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:37,090
Where's the daddy eagle?

30
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:44,190
My dad's gone, too.

31
00:10:00,470 --> 00:10:03,640
Help! Someone, help! 
McLeach took a little boy.

32
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,140
Send for help!

33
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:15,980
Code red, code red! Attention 
all Rescue Aid Society delegates.

34
00:12:16,060 --> 00:12:19,360
<i>All delegates report immediately 
to the main assembly hall.</i>

35
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:21,190
<i>This is an emergency meeting.</i>

36
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:24,530
<i>I repeat, this is a code red 
emergency meeting!</i>

37
00:12:27,030 --> 00:12:28,370
<i>Order!</i>

38
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:32,250
<i>Yes, I know it's late, but I'm... 
Really? Pajamas?</i>

39
00:12:32,330 --> 00:12:34,870
<i>Hello, Frank, how are you? 
Nice to see you!</i>

40
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:36,710
<i>And Esmerelda, there you are!</i>

41
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:39,590
<i>Quiet now, please, 
everyone pay attention.</i>

42
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:42,420
<i>There has been 
a kidnapping in Australia.</i>

43
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:45,340
<i>A young boy needs our help.</i>

44
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:48,800
<i>This is a mission 
requiring our very finest,</i>

45
00:12:48,890 --> 00:12:53,180
<i>and I know we are all thinking 
of the same two mice.</i>

46
00:12:56,650 --> 00:12:58,770
<i>What's this? Gone?</i>

47
00:12:58,860 --> 00:13:02,900
<i>We must find Bernard 
and Miss Bianca at once!</i>

48
00:13:15,210 --> 00:13:17,170
Pea soup.

49
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:29,350
Pea soup!

50
00:13:44,530 --> 00:13:48,910
To my dear Bernard, 
and our wonderful partnership.

51
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:52,660
Yeah, wonderful.

52
00:13:55,500 --> 00:14:00,330
You've been very quiet this evening. 
ls there something on your mind?

53
00:14:00,670 --> 00:14:03,000
Well, actually...

54
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:07,010
- I was wondering... 
- Yes, darling?

55
00:14:07,550 --> 00:14:10,180
I... Miss Bianca, would you...

56
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:12,970
Would you...

57
00:14:13,350 --> 00:14:15,430
Would you excuse me for a minute?

58
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:37,080
<i>Pardonnez-moi, Mademoiselle Bianca,</i> 
I <i>have important news.</i>

59
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:38,960
Yes, Frangois? What is it?

60
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:41,670
You and Bernard 
have been asked to accept

61
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:44,250
a dangerous mission to Australia.

62
00:14:44,590 --> 00:14:48,630
The poor boy. This is dreadful.

63
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:51,510
Now where is Bernard? 
I must tell him at once!

64
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:55,220
Allow me, madame, 
I will tell him immediately.

65
00:15:13,410 --> 00:15:14,780
Miss Bianca, will you marry me?

66
00:15:14,870 --> 00:15:18,000
Quickly, Monsieur Bernard! 
I must speak with you.

67
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:21,750
- Not now, Frangois, I'm busy! 
- No, monsieur, you don't...

68
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:29,380
- Bernard, did you talk to Frangois? 
- Yes, but there's something I want...

69
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:32,970
I know what you're going to say. 
Frangois told me about it.

70
00:15:33,180 --> 00:15:34,220
He did? How did he...

71
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:37,770
it doesn't matter, 
I think it's a marvelous idea.

72
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:39,140
You do?

73
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:41,310
I mean, you really want to?

74
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:45,650
I don't think it's a matter of wanting, 
it's a matter of duty.

75
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:49,030
Duty? I never thought of it...

76
00:15:49,110 --> 00:15:52,860
Well, all right. 
How does next April sound to you?

77
00:15:52,950 --> 00:15:56,700
Heavens, no! 
We must act immediately, tonight!

78
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:59,660
Tonight? But wait!

79
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:04,750
Bianca, this is so sudden. I mean, don't 
you at least need a gown or something?

80
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:08,840
No, just a pair of khaki shorts 
and some hiking boots!

81
00:16:09,090 --> 00:16:10,260
Hiking boots?

82
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:12,590
There you are.

83
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,930
Come along, come along.

84
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:22,140
<i>Delegates, we have 
an important announcement.</i>

85
00:16:22,270 --> 00:16:27,150
<i>Bernard and I have decided 
to accept the mission to Australia.</i>

86
00:16:27,230 --> 00:16:28,230
Australia?

87
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:31,780
Good show! 
Now, you must fly out immediately!

88
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:35,450
It's a little nippy outside, 
but we won't let that stop us, will we?

89
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:51,800
Miss Bianca, 
I'm not sure it's a good idea

90
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,880
to fly this soon after eating!

91
00:16:53,970 --> 00:16:56,390
Darling, you'll be just fine!

92
00:16:56,550 --> 00:16:59,680
But aren't you supposed 
to wait 45 minutes?

93
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:04,940
Just knock on the door 
and see if Orville is there!

94
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:10,860
Nobody's home, let's go.

95
00:17:11,070 --> 00:17:15,900
This is no time to play in the snow.

96
00:17:16,570 --> 00:17:19,660
I wasn't playing in the snow. 
It was an avalanche.

97
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:21,870
Look, Bernard!

98
00:17:21,950 --> 00:17:24,910
"Under new management, see Wilbur."

99
00:17:29,170 --> 00:17:32,170
Come on, darling. Let's get a move out!

100
00:17:45,430 --> 00:17:46,940
<i>I'm the cat's pajamas</i>

101
00:17:47,020 --> 00:17:49,230
<i>Always run around 
with crazy little mamas</i>

102
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:52,940
Mr. Wilbur!

103
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,740
Get down there, son!

104
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:55,900
Hello?

105
00:17:56,570 --> 00:17:59,780
Pick it, boy, pick it! Yeah!

106
00:18:02,660 --> 00:18:05,120
Here we go! Let's walk!

107
00:18:08,210 --> 00:18:10,790
Look out! Excuse me, sir.

108
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:14,460
Do something! He can't hear us!

109
00:18:14,630 --> 00:18:16,760
Big time, big time!

110
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:20,390
<i>The girls all look when I go by...</i>

111
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:22,600
Who killed the music?

112
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:23,850
That's better.

113
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:28,890
Excuse us for interrupting. 
We're from the Rescue Aid Society.

114
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:31,730
I am Miss Bianca, and this is my...

115
00:18:31,810 --> 00:18:34,230
The Miss Bianca? I don't believe it.

116
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:38,740
My brother, Orville, told me all about 
you. Boy. This is an honor to have...

117
00:18:38,990 --> 00:18:42,160
<i>May</i> I <i>just say, "Enchanté, sefiorita, "</i> 
to <i>you? May</i> I?

118
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:47,080
We need to charter a flight.

119
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:50,870
You've come to the right place, 
buddy boy. Welcome to...

120
00:18:51,250 --> 00:18:54,750
"Albatross Air. 
A fair fare from here to there."

121
00:18:55,420 --> 00:18:58,670
Get it? A fair fare? 
It's a play on... Never mind.

122
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:01,840
I've got tons of exotic 
destinations, faraway places,

123
00:19:02,140 --> 00:19:05,720
custom designed for 
a romantic weekend getaway.

124
00:19:06,390 --> 00:19:08,560
The finest in-flight accommodations.

125
00:19:08,850 --> 00:19:11,140
Speaking of which, what can I get you?

126
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:14,940
How about a nice mango Maui cooler? 
Very nice, very tasty.

127
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:16,190
No, thank you.

128
00:19:17,610 --> 00:19:20,200
A coconut, guava nectar? 
It's carbonated.

129
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:23,450
I got little umbrellas for each one, 
and a little coconut thing.

130
00:19:23,530 --> 00:19:27,040
- It's urgent that we leave immediately! 
- Nothing? Nothing at all?

131
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:30,580
- How about a cream soda? 
- We need a flight to Australia.

132
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:32,960
Australia? The land down under?

133
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:36,590
That's a fabulous idea! 
So when can I pencil you in?

134
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:39,720
After spring thaw? 
Mid-June would be very nice.

135
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:41,800
We must leave tonight.

136
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:44,640
Tonight?

137
00:19:46,350 --> 00:19:48,100
Come on, you're kidding me, right?

138
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:51,310
Have you looked outside? 
It's suicide out there.

139
00:19:51,390 --> 00:19:54,150
No. No.

140
00:19:54,230 --> 00:19:57,270
I'm afraid yourjolly little holiday 
will have to wait.

141
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:58,730
What a bunch of jokers.

142
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:02,570
But you don't understand, 
a boy needs our help. He's in trouble.

143
00:20:02,650 --> 00:20:05,870
Boy? You mean, a little kid kinda boy?

144
00:20:05,950 --> 00:20:07,200
He was kidnapped.

145
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:11,080
Kidnapped? That's awful.

146
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:13,370
Locking up a little kid.

147
00:20:13,670 --> 00:20:15,000
A kid should be free.

148
00:20:15,250 --> 00:20:18,210
Free to run wild through the house 
on Saturday mornings.

149
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:22,130
Free to have cookies and milk, 
and get those little white mustaches.

150
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:25,680
Nobody's gonna take 
a kid's freedom away while I'm around.

151
00:20:25,970 --> 00:20:28,220
Does that mean you'll take us?

152
00:20:28,430 --> 00:20:33,600
Storm or no storm, 
Albatross Airlines, at your service!

153
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:37,110
Passengers are requested 
to fasten their seat belts

154
00:20:37,190 --> 00:20:38,610
and secure all carry-ens.

155
00:20:38,730 --> 00:20:43,070
We'll be departing following our 
pre-flight maintenance. Thank you.

156
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:46,910
Loosen up, get the blood flowing 
up to the head.

157
00:20:46,990 --> 00:20:49,280
And a couple of these...

158
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:52,250
Okay, one's enough, there we go.

159
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,210
Yeah! That feels better. Baby.

160
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:59,670
Tie your kangaroos down, sports fans!

161
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:02,340
Here we come!

162
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:07,390
Let's go for it! Hey! 
I didn't adjust for the winds.

163
00:21:07,470 --> 00:21:10,390
All right, we're gonna make it! 
Gotta duck down lower.

164
00:21:10,470 --> 00:21:14,020
Go under the wind, go under it! 
Here we go!

165
00:21:15,140 --> 00:21:16,980
This is cold!

166
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:20,270
Slippery! Ice!

167
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:21,730
We got ice!

168
00:21:21,980 --> 00:21:23,990
Hang on now!

169
00:21:26,910 --> 00:21:28,530
Here we go!

170
00:21:29,660 --> 00:21:35,080
Cowabunga!

171
00:21:40,170 --> 00:21:44,210
Captain, is this 
a non-stop flight to Australia?

172
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:48,090
Well, not exactly no. 
I could definitely say no.

173
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:51,010
We're gonna have to make 
connections with a bigger bird.

174
00:21:51,180 --> 00:21:54,310
Non-stop? What do I look like, 
Charles Lindbergh?

175
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:03,440
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, Flight 12 
is now approaching Sydney airport.</i>

176
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:06,570
<i>Make sure your seat belts 
are fastened and tables secured.</i>

177
00:22:06,650 --> 00:22:08,860
<i>Enjoy your stay in Australia.</i>

178
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:15,330
- Are we there yet? 
- Yes.

179
00:22:15,410 --> 00:22:17,500
Perhaps we should wake up Wilbur.

180
00:22:17,830 --> 00:22:20,000
All right, I'll get him up.

181
00:22:20,540 --> 00:22:22,210
Wilbur.

182
00:22:24,050 --> 00:22:25,170
Wilbur!

183
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:27,470
Just five more minutes, Ma.

184
00:22:27,550 --> 00:22:30,090
- Wilbur! 
- That's all I need, five more minutes.

185
00:22:30,510 --> 00:22:33,350
Wilbur, are you awake?

186
00:22:33,430 --> 00:22:35,850
- Get up, we're there! 
- I'm up, I'm up.

187
00:22:35,930 --> 00:22:37,350
Watch out!

188
00:22:38,770 --> 00:22:41,230
Must have been sleeping on a bolt.

189
00:22:43,230 --> 00:22:45,030
Oh, boy.

190
00:22:45,190 --> 00:22:48,320
Throw another shrimp on the barbie, 
'cause here I come!

191
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:52,490
- Here we go again! 
- Cannonball!

192
00:22:57,290 --> 00:23:00,330
Gangway! Coming through. 
Mice on board!

193
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:02,670
Clear the way! 
Move over madam, there you go!

194
00:23:02,750 --> 00:23:05,130
Coming through, sir. Thank you.

195
00:23:09,010 --> 00:23:11,090
Next stop, Mugwomp Flats.

196
00:23:11,220 --> 00:23:14,010
Did we lose anyone back there?

197
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:17,850
Miss Bianca, from now on, 
can't we just take the train?

198
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:31,910
Well, Sparky, 
you've had this coming for a long time.

199
00:23:32,410 --> 00:23:34,280
And now, you're gonna get it.

200
00:23:44,540 --> 00:23:45,840
Wise fly.

201
00:23:47,590 --> 00:23:48,800
<i>Mugwomp tower,</i>

202
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:53,470
<i>this is Albatross 1-3 
requesting permission to land. Over?</i>

203
00:23:53,590 --> 00:23:56,470
Albatross? Let's see.

204
00:23:56,970 --> 00:23:58,520
Finch, wren, scrub-bird, lorikeet,

205
00:23:58,600 --> 00:24:00,560
freckled duck, galah, 
Kookaburra, parrot,

206
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:03,650
cockatoo, alba... It's a jumbo!

207
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:05,980
Negative, you'll have to turn back.

208
00:24:06,060 --> 00:24:09,320
- Our runway isn't long enough for you. 
- Not long enough?

209
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:12,070
<i>Look pal, 
I can land this thing on a dime!</i>

210
00:24:12,150 --> 00:24:14,820
<i>Wilbur, 
if the runway isn't long enough...</i>

211
00:24:14,910 --> 00:24:18,080
<i>You can't let radar jockeys 
push you around. Leave it to me.</i>

212
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:22,210
I say again, mate, 
our runway is too short.

213
00:24:22,290 --> 00:24:25,830
<i>And I say again, mate, I'm coming in!</i>

214
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:29,340
Crazy Yank. Quick, Sparky, 
we gotta extend the runway.

215
00:24:34,260 --> 00:24:35,760
Here we go!

216
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:37,300
We'll never make it!

217
00:24:41,390 --> 00:24:42,850
Hot!

218
00:24:43,350 --> 00:24:45,270
Passengers, please remain seated

219
00:24:45,350 --> 00:24:48,020
until the aircraft comes 
to a full and complete stop.

220
00:24:48,110 --> 00:24:49,770
Thank you.

221
00:24:56,530 --> 00:24:58,870
Quick, Sparky, 
we need to make a drag line!

222
00:25:10,500 --> 00:25:13,920
Don't try and tell me 
the runway's too short.

223
00:25:14,130 --> 00:25:16,260
Hold this for me, will you, pal?

224
00:25:20,390 --> 00:25:22,220
Bloke ought to have his wings clipped.

225
00:25:22,310 --> 00:25:25,140
Captain thanks you 
for flying Albatross Airlines...

226
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:26,690
Crazy Yanks.

227
00:25:26,770 --> 00:25:29,940
They think they can do any fool thing 
without regard for...

228
00:25:40,740 --> 00:25:42,620
Welcome to Australia, ma'am.

229
00:25:42,700 --> 00:25:45,910
Name's Jake. If there's any way 
I can make your stay pleasant,

230
00:25:46,920 --> 00:25:48,250
don't hesitate to ask.

231
00:25:48,330 --> 00:25:51,590
- How kind. 
- Allow me to get that bag for you.

232
00:25:52,670 --> 00:25:55,920
I've got a lot of luggage here.

233
00:25:56,050 --> 00:25:57,840
Let me give you a hand with those.

234
00:25:57,930 --> 00:26:00,140
Part of the friendly service 
at Albatross...

235
00:26:01,350 --> 00:26:02,560
Big time hurt!

236
00:26:02,640 --> 00:26:04,020
Back! It's out!

237
00:26:04,100 --> 00:26:07,100
- Are you all right? 
- Don't worry, I'll handle this.

238
00:26:07,190 --> 00:26:10,520
Sparky, watch the tower. 
We gotta get this bird to the hospital.

239
00:26:10,610 --> 00:26:14,110
Can't go down, can't go up. 
Take the bags!

240
00:26:14,280 --> 00:26:16,490
Now we just gotta 
figure out how to get there.

241
00:26:16,570 --> 00:26:21,280
So are you and your husband here 
on a little outback excursion?

242
00:26:21,370 --> 00:26:23,370
No, we're not married.

243
00:26:25,540 --> 00:26:28,790
In fact, we're here 
on a top secret mission.

244
00:26:28,870 --> 00:26:30,500
Very hush-hush.

245
00:26:31,210 --> 00:26:33,250
Gonna rescue that kid 
McLeach nabbed?

246
00:26:33,340 --> 00:26:35,960
Why, that's right! How did you know?

247
00:26:36,050 --> 00:26:39,550
You'll find it's tough 
to keep secrets in the outback, miss.

248
00:26:39,840 --> 00:26:42,350
So which way you taking?

249
00:26:42,470 --> 00:26:45,930
Suicide Trail through Nightmare 
Canyon, or shortcut at Satan's Ridge?

250
00:26:46,020 --> 00:26:48,230
-"Suicide Trail"? 
- Good choice.

251
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:50,810
More snakes, less quicksand.

252
00:26:50,900 --> 00:26:55,030
Then once you cross Bloodworm Creek, 
you're scat-free, that is until...

253
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:56,740
Dead Dingo Pass.

254
00:26:56,820 --> 00:27:01,240
Wait a minute, I don't see 
any of that stuff on the map.

255
00:27:01,320 --> 00:27:03,280
A map's no good in the outback!

256
00:27:03,570 --> 00:27:08,160
What you really need is someone 
who knows the territory.

257
00:27:08,250 --> 00:27:10,830
Mr. Jake, will you guide us?

258
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:12,830
At your service!

259
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:16,500
Better take my arm, miss. 
It's gonna be a treacherous hike.

260
00:27:16,590 --> 00:27:20,680
I remember the time it was just me 
and 400 of these big, giant...

261
00:27:20,760 --> 00:27:23,760
Doesn't even know how to fold a map.

262
00:27:29,430 --> 00:27:32,400
This is how we get around 
in the outback, Miss B.

263
00:27:33,100 --> 00:27:35,730
The only way to travel, Berno.

264
00:27:35,820 --> 00:27:39,360
Yeah, it's just a little bumpy back here.

265
00:27:45,910 --> 00:27:49,450
Cinch up your seat belts, mates. 
We're coming in for a landing.

266
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:55,630
Hold it, not yet!

267
00:28:10,430 --> 00:28:11,600
Maybe I should go...

268
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:15,110
Maybe I should go look for him.

269
00:28:15,270 --> 00:28:18,650
Don't you worry about Jake. 
He can handle himself.

270
00:28:19,150 --> 00:28:20,440
Yeah, I noticed.

271
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:23,200
I am just sure he'll be back in no time.

272
00:28:31,620 --> 00:28:35,830
You know, 
now that we're alone, there's...

273
00:28:35,960 --> 00:28:39,420
There's something that 
I've been wanting to ask you.

274
00:28:39,500 --> 00:28:41,460
Yes? What is it?

275
00:28:41,550 --> 00:28:44,630
Well, it's like this.

276
00:28:44,970 --> 00:28:49,560
Miss Bianca, I would be most honored

277
00:28:50,520 --> 00:28:52,060
if...

278
00:28:52,180 --> 00:28:54,060
Look out!

279
00:28:58,400 --> 00:29:01,190
No mice for you, Twister, not today!

280
00:29:01,320 --> 00:29:02,320
There!

281
00:29:03,740 --> 00:29:05,110
Miss Bianca!

282
00:29:05,200 --> 00:29:07,740
I've been looking all over for you.

283
00:29:07,820 --> 00:29:09,450
Now look.

284
00:29:09,830 --> 00:29:13,290
We got a long way to go, 
and you're gonna take us there.

285
00:29:13,410 --> 00:29:16,040
You're not gonna give us 
any trouble about it.

286
00:29:16,790 --> 00:29:18,750
Right?

287
00:29:19,210 --> 00:29:21,210
Jake's been gone...

288
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:24,220
They're harmless once you look them 
in the eye, let them know who's boss.

289
00:29:22,550 --> 00:29:24,720
Been gone a long time.

290
00:29:24,300 --> 00:29:27,090
Ain't that right, mate? Now get.

291
00:29:27,180 --> 00:29:31,930
It's all right, Bernard. 
Jake has everything under control.

292
00:29:32,020 --> 00:29:34,560
Yeah, I noticed.

293
00:29:36,190 --> 00:29:40,690
You know, Miss Bianca, truth be told, 
I used to be quite a dingo wrestler.

294
00:29:41,110 --> 00:29:44,030
There was this one time, 
it was just me and 300

295
00:29:44,150 --> 00:29:46,650
of these ferocious, 
mouse-eating dingoes.

296
00:29:46,740 --> 00:29:49,030
Had me surrounded...

297
00:29:59,750 --> 00:30:01,630
Show him who's boss, Berno!

298
00:30:29,530 --> 00:30:31,530
Okay, you guys, she fell for it.

299
00:30:32,910 --> 00:30:34,620
Looks like the coast is clear.

300
00:30:35,450 --> 00:30:37,710
Girls? Girls, I'm here!

301
00:30:39,540 --> 00:30:41,920
Where are you, you little chickees, you?

302
00:30:42,250 --> 00:30:43,590
Wilbur?

303
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:45,260
Wilbur!

304
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,840
Don't ever do that to me again!

305
00:30:50,800 --> 00:30:53,430
Boy, I lost a lot of feathers on that one.

306
00:30:53,510 --> 00:30:55,600
Wilbur, am I glad to see you!

307
00:30:55,770 --> 00:30:58,270
- Help me with these eggs, will you? 
- Sure.

308
00:30:58,600 --> 00:31:01,600
Wait a minute, what the heck 
are you doing up here?

309
00:31:01,770 --> 00:31:05,190
The kidnapper took the boy and Jake. 
Miss Bianca.

310
00:31:05,280 --> 00:31:06,860
Miss Bianca's in trouble?

311
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:13,030
That's terrible! We gotta do something! 
Bernard, I'm disappointed in you.

312
00:31:13,120 --> 00:31:15,030
Hiding under a nest 
while Bianca needs help.

313
00:31:15,410 --> 00:31:17,870
- I gotta talk to you, mister. 
- Wilbur.

314
00:31:17,950 --> 00:31:22,420
You should start searching the desert 
for her, and I'll scan the coastline!

315
00:31:22,500 --> 00:31:25,000
That's what I'll do. 
Ask the chicks on the beach.

316
00:31:25,090 --> 00:31:26,130
What?

317
00:31:26,210 --> 00:31:29,260
Listen! There's some chicks 
here that need help.

318
00:31:29,340 --> 00:31:31,090
Really?

319
00:31:34,100 --> 00:31:36,720
No. Wait a minute. Hold it.

320
00:31:36,930 --> 00:31:40,140
I know what you're thinking, 
and you're wrong. Don't even, no.

321
00:31:40,980 --> 00:31:43,690
Don't look at me! You're getting "no." 
Understand?

322
00:31:43,770 --> 00:31:45,900
I will not ever sit on those eggs!

323
00:31:47,070 --> 00:31:48,480
Nuts!

324
00:31:50,360 --> 00:31:53,360
Gotta learn to be more assertive. 
No is no is no.

325
00:31:54,490 --> 00:31:55,660
Hey, quit moving in there!

326
00:31:55,660 --> 00:31:55,700
Hey, quit moving in there!

327
00:32:11,630 --> 00:32:13,010
Oh, my gosh!

328
00:32:49,500 --> 00:32:50,760
Excuse me.

329
00:32:53,590 --> 00:32:56,760
Look, I've got a long way to go, 
you're going to take me there,

330
00:32:56,840 --> 00:32:59,510
and you're not going 
to give me any trouble, right?

331
00:33:03,180 --> 00:33:04,350
Good.

332
00:33:06,480 --> 00:33:07,860
NOW, get!

333
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:29,210
Help! Help!

334
00:34:00,700 --> 00:34:01,080
It's okay.

335
00:34:02,540 --> 00:34:04,200
Come on.

336
00:34:06,410 --> 00:34:07,870
Thanks, little mate.

337
00:34:11,670 --> 00:34:17,550
Bernard, you are magnificent. 
You are absolutely the hero of the day.

338
00:34:17,840 --> 00:34:21,050
Miss Bianca, 
before anything else happens,

339
00:34:23,180 --> 00:34:25,890
-will you marry me? 
- Bernard.

340
00:34:25,980 --> 00:34:28,480
Of course, I will!

341
00:34:29,980 --> 00:34:31,400
Well done, mate.

342
00:34:31,770 --> 00:34:35,570
Come on, Marahute, let's all go home.

343
00:34:57,840 --> 00:34:58,930
Help!

344
00:34:59,010 --> 00:35:00,590
Anybody!

345
00:35:00,930 --> 00:35:02,550
Bernard!

346
00:35:02,930 --> 00:35:04,890
Bianca!

347
00:35:04,970 --> 00:35:07,270
Where are you?

348
00:35:07,680 --> 00:35:10,900
Okay, that's it, I'm out of here. 
This is ridiculous.

349
00:35:10,980 --> 00:35:13,310
You can't leave me here alone.

350
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:15,530
I'm gone! I am gone.

351
00:35:17,820 --> 00:35:21,320
No, stay in those eggs! 
That's a direct order!

352
00:35:24,280 --> 00:35:28,000
Hey, you're kind of a cute little feller.
